Don't abort when the deadlock protector is contended (QTBUG-141579).

The render thread calls eglSurface() from swapBuffers(); if another thread
(typically QAndroidInputContext::runOnQtThread(), also the event dispatcher's
suspend path) holds the process-wide protector at that moment, Qt >= 6.9
qFatal()s. Qt <= 6.8 returned the existing surface here; QEGLPlatformContext::
swapBuffers() then skips the swap on EGL_NO_SURFACE, and the surface is
recreated on the next expose. Restore that behaviour.

--- a/qtbase/src/plugins/platforms/android/qandroidplatformopenglwindow.cpp
+++ b/qtbase/src/plugins/platforms/android/qandroidplatformopenglwindow.cpp
@@ -61,7 +61,8 @@
         static constexpr char funcName[] = "QAndroidPlatformOpenGLWindow::eglSurface()";
         QtAndroidPrivate::AndroidDeadlockProtector protector(funcName);
         if (!protector.acquire()) {
-            qFatal("Failed to acquire deadlock protector for %s.", funcName);
+            // QTBUG-141579: contention is transient, skip the frame instead of aborting
+            qWarning("Failed to acquire deadlock protector for %s.", funcName);
             return m_eglSurface;
         }

